{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Next Step"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Thanks, Everybody!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "  Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le15ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reason Clauses: Due to, because of, owing to <br/>Result Clauses: So \u2026 that"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Remember, when you want to introduce a reason for a particular situation, you can use these prepositions at the beginning of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">because of</span></span> before a noun or a noun phrase.</li><li><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">Due to</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">owing to</span></span> also mean <span class=\"italic\">because of</span>. They sound a little more formal, and are therefore more common in professional English rather than conversational.</li><li>When you want to link a cause with a result, you can use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">so ... that</span></span>. You normally use an adjective or adverb after so. </li><li>Remember than in formal English, you can put <span class=\"italic\">So ... that </span>at the beginning of the sentence and put the verb before the object.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember than in formal English, you can put <span class=\"italic\">So ... that </span>at the beginning of the sentence and put the verb before the object."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd say that <span class=\"strong\">because of </span>some really hard work the launch was a great success! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There were a few snags <span class=\"strong\">due to</span> unforeseen events but we pulled together and we pulled it off."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was discovered at the last minute that <span class=\"strong\">owing to</span> illness, the speaker was unable to attend so we had to arrange for someone else."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He is so well-versed on the subject of social media <span class=\"strong\">that </span>he was able to come and speak without much advance notice. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The author was very happy and said that <span class=\"strong\">because of</span> the way we handled her launch, she hopes to work with us on her next book."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Report Verbs with Impersonal Passive Construction"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to report a fact or belief, you can use a variety of ways to construct your ideas. When you do not want to mention the source of the information, you can use a passive structure.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the structure <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">It + passive verb + that + finite clause</span></span>. <br/> A finite clause contain a verb which shows tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It was reported </span>that the army was crossing the frontier. </span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It has been shown </span>that the theory is correct.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is proposed</span> that prices should increase next year.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The following are report verbs you can use: <span class=\"italic\">admit, declare, hope propose, show, agree, discover, intend prove, state, allege, establish, know, recommend, suggest, announce, estimate, mention, regret, suppose, assume, expect, notice report, think, believe, explain, object, request, understand, claim, fear, observe, reveal, consider, feel, presume, say, discover, find, promise and see.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was understood that this was your first launch for us. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Thomas was available and it was revealed that he is a very knowledgeable and entertaining speaker."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was observed that you were a great assistant during the preparation and execution of the launch."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was also decided that we would extend the print run of the book."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is agreed that the launch was a wonderful success!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "venue"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "\u200bplace where  large or important \u200bevents \u200bhappen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The venue was great. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words to review. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reaction"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "\u200bbehavior, a \u200bfeeling, or an \u200baction that is a \u200bdirect \u200bresult of something \u200belse"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm really happy with the reaction from the crowd. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "requirement"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a thing that is compulsory; a necessary condition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There were a few extra requirements due to unforeseen events."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "on track"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "making progress and likely to succeed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  We pulled together and we got back on track."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "alternate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one that can take the \u200bplace of another"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We had to arrange for an alternate speaker."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "engaging"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pleasant, interesting, and attractive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He is a very engaging and entertaining speaker."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to arrange for"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to \u200bplan, \u200bprepare for, or \u200borganize something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It was observed that you were a great assistant during the preparation and arranging for the launch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le15ob11aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ask someone to tell you about an event they attended that was successfully organized and run."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down what aspects of the event were successful and the reasons that it was successful."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down any aspects of the event that were not totally successful."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the information you got from the person you talked to to make a checklist of things to do to organize and host a successful event."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I interview someone about a successful event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write notes on what was successful and why it was successful."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write notes on what was not successful."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the information I gathered to make a list of things to do to have a successful event."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exer